# What `podman build` may see, now that the context is the repository root.
#
# The context widened from `backend/` to `.` so the image could build the
# interface (see the header of `backend/Containerfile`). That change hands the
# builder everything in the tree unless it is excluded here, which is both a
# speed problem and a disclosure one: a build context is uploaded whole, and
# anything in it can end up in a layer through a careless `COPY`.
#
# The Containerfile copies by explicit path and never `COPY . .`, so nothing
# below can reach an image by accident today. This file is the second control,
# for the day somebody adds a broader COPY.

# Version control and CI metadata.
.git/
.github/
.gitea/
.gitignore
.containerignore

# Never in a build context, let alone an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image, and
# `node_modules` alone is hundreds of megabytes of context for nothing.
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
frontend/dist/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# Not part of any artefact.
docs/
ops/
homeassistant/
tools/
assets/
backend/tests/
*.md
!frontend/README.md

# Editor and OS noise.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
